<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT- Chemical companies downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT- Chemical companies downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said analyst Paul Leming downgraded Dow Chemical Co, Union Carbide Corp and Lyondell Petrochemical Co to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- In a research report, he said in the third quarter margins in ethylene and polyethylene should decline &quot;precipitously&quot; and the ethylene industry is moving into a trough. Another period of peak profitability may not occur until 2004.</p>
<p>-- Union Carbide dipped 3/8 to 47-3/8 in early trading.</p>
<p>-- Dow Chemical fell 1-1/8 to 85-1/4.</p>
<p>-- Lyondell lost 1/4 to 22-3/8.</p>
</text>
